diff --git a/docs/GUIDE.md b/docs/GUIDE.md
index 9800535..b497d00 100644
--- a/docs/GUIDE.md
+++ b/docs/GUIDE.md
@@ -689,6 +689,25 @@ stay in sync:
 
 ## Claude Code sessions
 
+### The New screen and the default harness
+
+⌘N (or **New session**) opens the New screen instead of an empty session: a greeting with your Mac
+account's first name (read locally from the account's full name), a large composer, and the settings
+for the session it will make: **Chat only** or **Folder** (the folder chip; recent folders show as
+pills below), the Claude model, effort, mode (Plan / Ask / Accept edits) and **Tools** (skills). Nothing
+is created until you Send; if that first message fails, your text and attachments stay in the composer.
+
+New sessions run on the Claude Code harness, your own Claude subscription:
+`[sessions].default_harness = "claude_code"` (set it to `"builtin"` for the API-key loop). If the
+claude CLI isn't installed the session falls back to the built-in loop; a notice on the New screen says
+so, or tells you to run `claude auth login`. Scheduled tasks, campaigns, fleet and subagents always use
+the built-in loop, and existing sessions keep their harness.
+
+Chat-only sessions work in a private per-session folder (`sessions/<id>/work`, owner-only). Chat-only
+sessions from before this keep `sessions/<id>`, so `claude --resume` still finds their conversation.
+Workflows aren't offered in Claude subscription sessions: they need the built-in loop with an API key.
+
+
 Checked against claude 2.1.308 logged in with a claude.ai (Max) subscription; the redacted captures
 are in `tests/fixtures/claude_stream/` and the test CLI replays them. A later Claude Code release can
 change these details: see Troubleshooting.
